  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Towards a Climate Adaptation Model in Putumayo-Ic&#xe1;</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Strengthen climate resilience and food security of indigenous communities in Amazon Basin through an integrated climate adaptation model promoting health and well-being through sustainable food systems. The ACT project will directly benefit 518 people from the Putumayo Amazon communities, and indirectly will reach around 1,025 members of neighbouring communities from other indigenous peoples who will incorporate the learning and practices derived from the chagras (traditional agroforestry systems) and the fish farming pilots, expanding the dissemination of knowledge and reinforcing the collective sustainability of the food systems. Strengthening traditional governance and knowledge systems is a central feature of the project to support the protection of Amazon rainforest and its cultures.</narrative>
  </description>
